course: dictionary
lesson: 6627
title: Notice: seeing, signs and attention
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Notice has several meanings, and the words around it show you which one. «A boy in Halifax squints at the board and sits closer and closer; his teacher notices.» Here notice means sees or becomes aware of something. Ask: what word would fit here? Try "sees" in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Notice can also be a noun, a written sign or message. «Put a notice on the board» means a sign that gives information. Notice can also mean a warning given in advance: «at short notice» means with very little warning. Look at the words next to notice to choose the right meaning.
explain: Notice can mean paying attention. «Take no notice» means do not pay attention to something. «Tiny words like "please" and "thank you" make people feel noticed» means that people feel seen and cared about. Clues like these help you work out meaning without a dictionary.
fact: Notice means to see, hear or become aware of something.
fact: As a noun, a notice is a written sign or message giving information.
fact: «At short notice» means with only a little warning.
fact: «Take no notice» means do not pay attention to something.
fact: In science, noticing means observing: seeing patterns and changes.
exercise: «A boy in Halifax squints at the board, and his teacher notices.» What does notices mean here? | Throws away | Writes a message about | Forgets all about | *Sees or becomes aware of
exercise: «Put a notice on the board.» What is a notice in this sentence? | A loud noise | *A written sign or message giving information | A picture of a person | A kind of board game
exercise: «The trip was changed at short notice.» What does short notice mean? | For a very short time only | *With very little warning | Near the door | At the very end of the day
test: «Languages keep changing, so notice odd words and ask what they mean.» Which meaning of notice fits here? | A written sign or message | *To see or become aware of | Attention given to a person | A warning given in advance
test: Which phrase means do not pay attention to something? | At short notice | Until further notice | *Take no notice | Notice board
exam: «Gran hands Sam a present, and Mum raises an eyebrow.» Which words in the sentence show that Mum is noticing Sam? | Gran is smiling | Sam is holding a present | *Mum raises an eyebrow | Gran hands Sam a present
